Bazel Remote Execution API (REAPI) v2 — wire-compatible protocol definitions
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream:  https://github.com/bazelbuild/remote-apis
Copyright: The Bazel Authors
License:   Apache-2.0

Files:
  source/engine/distributed/protocol/proto/reapi_compat.proto

Declares `package build.bazel.remote.execution.v2` and the upstream
`go_package` option because wire and namespace compatibility is the entire
point: it lets bldr talk to existing RE infrastructure (BuildBuddy, BuildBarn,
and similar). Message shapes follow the upstream schema. bldr substitutes
BLAKE3 where REAPI conventionally uses SHA-256.

